<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The rate card the client supplied (LIST_MDR.xlsx, 17 banks x 18 product columns),
     reduced to the 39 PAYMENT labels the stores' X70D export actually writes.

     Two things about this data are easy to "correct" and must not be:

     * QRIS at BCA, BNI and BRI is 0,00%, while MANDIRI and CIMB charge 0,70%. The
       zeros are real numbers in the source and were confirmed by the client on
       2026-09-18. QRIS is also the busiest tender there is (47% of transactions at
       Kelapa Gading), so assuming the regulated 0,70% instead would overstate the
       fee by about Rp 1,19 million per store per month.
     * BNI charges the same 1,10% on us and off us. Unusual, and what the card says.

     No date_from: the rate card carries no effective date. Empty means "as far back
     as there is data", which is right until Finance says from when these were
     agreed. Set date_from then, and add the older rates as separate rows rather than
     editing these: a rate is effective-dated so that reconciliations already done
     are not silently restated.

     Only the four acquirers that appear in the feed are seeded. The other thirteen
     banks on the card are card *issuers* on installment plans, and the PAYMENT label
     names only the acquirer ("BCA - 0% 3 Bln"), so an issuer-funded installment
     cannot be told apart from the acquirer's own rate. No installment transaction
     has been seen yet; confirm with Finance before the first one is.

     noupdate="1": rates are operational data. Once loaded they belong to Finance,
     and a module upgrade must not undo a renegotiation. -->
<odoo noupdate="1">

    <record id="rate_cash" model="levis.mdr.rate">
        <field name="payment">CASH</field>
        <field name="acquirer"></field>
        <field name="percent">0.0</field>
        <field name="note">Not a card tender: no acquirer, no fee.</field>
    </record>

